/** @page sshsftpbackendguide SFTP Backend Guide

    @tableofcontents

    @section sshsftpbackendoverview Backend Overview

    @ref Qore::Ssh::SftpSession "SftpSession" delegates all SFTP protocol
    operations to a pluggable backend object. The binary module handles packet
    encoding/decoding, handle bookkeeping, and channel lifecycle; the backend
    controls the visible path namespace, metadata, and content.

    A backend is attached by passing an \c sftp_factory_callback closure in
    @ref Qore::Ssh::SshServerConfig "SshServerConfig" (returns a backend per
    session) or by calling
    @ref Qore::Ssh::SftpSession::setBackend() "SftpSession::setBackend()".

    @section sshsftpbackendcontract Backend Contract

    A backend must implement at least \c stat() and \c list(). All other
    methods are optional; \c SftpSession uses \c backendHasMethod() to gate
    dispatch. When a method is absent, the module replies with
    \c SSH_FX_OP_UNSUPPORTED.

    <b>Required Methods</b>

    |!Method|!Request Type|!Result Type|!Purpose
    |\c stat()|@ref Qore::Ssh::SftpPathRequest "SftpPathRequest"|@ref Qore::Ssh::SftpPathInfo "SftpPathInfo"|Return file or directory metadata for a path
    |\c list()|@ref Qore::Ssh::SftpPathRequest "SftpPathRequest"|@ref Qore::Ssh::SftpListResult "SftpListResult"|Return directory listing entries

    <b>Optional Methods</b>

    |!Method|!Request Type|!Purpose
    |\c openRead()|@ref Qore::Ssh::SftpOpenRequest "SftpOpenRequest"|Open a file for reading
    |\c read()|@ref Qore::Ssh::SftpReadRequest "SftpReadRequest"|Streamed read chunk
    |\c closeRead()|@ref Qore::Ssh::SftpCloseRequest "SftpCloseRequest"|Finalize a streamed read
    |\c openWrite()|@ref Qore::Ssh::SftpOpenRequest "SftpOpenRequest"|Open a file for writing
    |\c write()|@ref Qore::Ssh::SftpWriteRequest "SftpWriteRequest"|Streamed write chunk
    |\c closeWrite()|@ref Qore::Ssh::SftpCloseRequest "SftpCloseRequest"|Finalize a write
    |\c removePath()|@ref Qore::Ssh::SftpPathRequest "SftpPathRequest"|Remove a file or symlink
    |\c rename()|@ref Qore::Ssh::SftpRenameRequest "SftpRenameRequest"|Rename or move a path
    |\c mkdir()|@ref Qore::Ssh::SftpPathRequest "SftpPathRequest"|Create a directory
    |\c rmdir()|@ref Qore::Ssh::SftpPathRequest "SftpPathRequest"|Remove a directory
    |\c symlink()|@ref Qore::Ssh::SftpSymlinkRequest "SftpSymlinkRequest"|Create a symbolic link
    |\c readlink()|@ref Qore::Ssh::SftpPathRequest "SftpPathRequest"|Read a symbolic link target
    |\c setstat()|@ref Qore::Ssh::SftpSetstatRequest "SftpSetstatRequest"|Set file attributes
    |\c statvfs()|@ref Qore::Ssh::SftpPathRequest "SftpPathRequest"|Filesystem statistics (\c statvfs\@openssh.com)

    @section sshsftpbackendstreaming Streamed vs Buffered Dispatch

    The \c openRead() return value controls the dispatch mode:

    - <b>Buffered</b>: \c openRead() returns \c data in
      @ref Qore::Ssh::SftpOpenResult "SftpOpenResult". The session sends the
      data immediately; no \c read() or \c closeRead() calls are made.
    - <b>Streamed</b>: \c openRead() returns a \c backend_handle without
      \c data. The session routes \c SSH_FXP_READ packets through \c read()
      and calls \c closeRead() on handle close. Both methods must be present.

    The same model applies to writes: a \c backend_handle from \c openWrite()
    enables streamed \c write() dispatch; otherwise the session accumulates the
    upload and passes complete data to \c closeWrite().

    @section sshsftpbackendvfs VirtualSftpFilesystem

    @ref SftpServerDataProvider::VirtualSftpFilesystem "VirtualSftpFilesystem"
    is an in-memory backend implementing the full contract, suitable for
    testing, serving generated content, and building virtual namespaces.

    Key features:
    - In-memory file/directory storage with configurable default permissions
    - Symlink support (\c symlink(), \c readlink(), symlink-aware \c stat())
    - Helpers: \c addFile(), \c addTextFile(), \c addDirectory(),
      \c getFileData(), \c getFileText(), \c getFilePaths()
    - Atomic exchange: \c submit(), \c listAvailable(), \c retrieve(),
      \c completeRetrieve()
    - Optional persistence and snapshot export/import

    @code
    SftpServerDataProvider::VirtualSftpFilesystem vfs();
    vfs.addDirectory("/reports");
    vfs.addTextFile("/reports/summary.txt", "Q1 results\n");
    # attach to an SftpSession
    session.setBackend(vfs);
    @endcode

    @section sshsftpbackendexchange VirtualSftpExchange

    @ref SftpServerDataProvider::VirtualSftpExchange "VirtualSftpExchange"
    extends @ref SftpServerDataProvider::VirtualSftpFilesystem "VirtualSftpFilesystem"
    with explicit inbound/outbound exchange semantics for managed file
    submission workflows, policy-enforced uploads, outbound claim/archive
    lifecycle, and event-driven integration.

    Key features:
    - Configurable layout (\c inbound_dir, \c outbound_dir, \c archive_dir,
      \c claim_dir)
    - Inbound policy via
      @ref SftpServerDataProvider::VirtualSftpInboundPolicy "VirtualSftpInboundPolicy"
      (glob/regex, size limits, content prefix, per-principal, custom callbacks)
    - Outbound helpers: \c addOutboundData(), \c listOutbound(),
      \c claimOutbound(), \c archiveOutbound(), \c deleteOutbound()
    - Event listeners, retention policies, live upload policy enforcement

    @code
    SftpServerDataProvider::VirtualSftpExchange exchange(
        <SftpServerDataProvider::VirtualSftpExchangeOptions>{
            "archive_dir": "/archive",
            "inbound_policy": <SftpServerDataProvider::VirtualSftpInboundPolicy>{
                "accept_filename_glob": "*.csv",
                "max_size": 10485760,
            },
        }
    );
    exchange.addOutboundData("report.csv", binary("a,b,c\n"));
    session.setBackend(exchange);
    @endcode

    @section sshsftpbackendrecordstore VirtualSftpExchangeRecordStore

    @ref SftpServerDataProvider::VirtualSftpExchangeRecordStore "VirtualSftpExchangeRecordStore"
    wraps a @ref SftpServerDataProvider::VirtualSftpExchange "VirtualSftpExchange"
    with record-oriented queue methods for integration code that works with named
    records and payloads rather than virtual filesystem paths.

    Key features:
    - Submit: \c submitInboundRecord(), \c submitInboundTextRecord()
    - List: \c listInboundRecords(), \c listOutboundRecords()
    - Retrieve and complete: \c retrieveInboundRecord(),
      \c claimOutboundRecord(), \c archiveOutboundRecord()
    - Records typed as
      @ref SftpServerDataProvider::VirtualSftpRecordInfo "VirtualSftpRecordInfo"

    @code
    SftpServerDataProvider::VirtualSftpExchangeRecordStore store();
    store.submitInboundRecord("order.json", binary("{\"id\": 1}"));
    list<hash<SftpServerDataProvider::VirtualSftpRecordInfo>> records
        = store.listInboundRecords();
    @endcode

    @section sshsftpbackendcustom Implementing a Custom Backend

    Define a class with at least \c stat() and \c list(); add optional methods
    for the operations you need.

    @code
    class MyReadOnlyBackend {
        hash<Qore::Ssh::SftpPathInfo> stat(hash<Qore::Ssh::SftpPathRequest> req) {
            return <Qore::Ssh::SftpPathInfo>{
                "path": req.path, "exists": True, "directory": req.path == "/",
                "size": 1024, "permissions": 0100444,
                "mtime": now_us().epochSeconds(), "atime": now_us().epochSeconds(),
            };
        }
        hash<Qore::Ssh::SftpListResult> list(hash<Qore::Ssh::SftpPathRequest> req) {
            return <Qore::Ssh::SftpListResult>{
                "path": req.path, "entries": ({
                    "filename": "data.bin", "directory": False, "size": 1024,
                    "long_name": "-r--r--r-- 1 root root 1024 Jan 01 00:00 data.bin",
                    "permissions": 0100444,
                    "mtime": now_us().epochSeconds(), "atime": now_us().epochSeconds(),
                },),
            };
        }
        hash<Qore::Ssh::SftpOpenResult> openRead(hash<Qore::Ssh::SftpOpenRequest> req) {
            return <Qore::Ssh::SftpOpenResult>{
                "path": req.path, "exists": True,
                "data": binary("file content"), "size": 12, "permissions": 0100444,
            };
        }
    }
    session.setBackend(new MyReadOnlyBackend());
    @endcode

    Any absent method causes \c SSH_FX_OP_UNSUPPORTED for the corresponding
    operation. In this example, write, remove, rename, mkdir, rmdir, symlink,
    readlink, setstat, and statvfs are all unsupported.

    @section sshsftpbackendpersistence Persistence

    @ref SftpServerDataProvider::VirtualSftpPersistenceBackend "VirtualSftpPersistenceBackend"
    provides durable state for VirtualSftpFilesystem. Configure via
    @ref SftpServerDataProvider::VirtualSftpPersistenceOptions "VirtualSftpPersistenceOptions":

    - \c persistence_dir -- local directory for snapshot files
    - \c persistence_mode -- \c "snapshot" (periodic bulk saves) or
      \c "write-through" (save after every mutation)
    - \c snapshot_interval_seconds -- periodic snapshot interval (default 60)
    - \c restore_on_construct -- restore state on construction

    Snapshots use JSON
    (@ref SftpServerDataProvider::VirtualSftpSnapshot "VirtualSftpSnapshot")
    with atomic writes (write to \c .tmp, then rename) to prevent corruption.
    @code
    SftpServerDataProvider::VirtualSftpFilesystem vfs(
        <SftpServerDataProvider::VirtualSftpFilesystemOptions>{"persistence":
            <SftpServerDataProvider::VirtualSftpPersistenceOptions>{
                "persistence_dir": "/var/lib/myapp/sftp-state",
                "persistence_mode": "write-through",
                "restore_on_construct": True,
            }});
    @endcode
*/
